.SH NAME
.PP
simpla - A simple linear algebra library written in C.\& 
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
#include <simpla\&.h>

#define MAT_TYPE float

int main(void) {
    sm A = mat_from((float[9]){1, 2, 3,
                               4, 5, 6,
                               7, 8, 9},
                    3, 3);
    sm B = mat_alloc(3, 3);
    sm C = mat_alloc(3, 3);

    mat_rand(B, 0, 1);
    mat_dot(C, A, B);
    mat_free(B);
    mat_free(C);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBsimpla\fR is a simple linear algebra library written in C.\& It provides simple function interfaces and concise implementation of linear algebra operations with quite a small sacrifice of performance.\&
.PP
The core data structure is \fBsm\fR, which stands for NOT for Sadism & Masochism BUT for \fBs\fRimple \fBm\fRatrix:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
typedef struct {
    MAT_TYPE* p;
    size_t rows; // number of rows
    size_t cols; // number of columns
    size_t stride; // specifically for slicing
} sm;
.fi
.RE
.PP
where MAT_TYPE is a user-defined macro used for indicating the data type the matrix should be using, with the default value float.\&
